[
  {
    "kind": 1,
    "language": "markdown",
    "value": "# LoT (Language of Things) - Complete Training Session\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary><strong>Navigation Menu - Click to Expand</strong></summary>\r\n\r\n### Getting Started\r\n- [Environment Setup](./00-setup/verify-environment.lotnb)\r\n\r\n### Beginner Level\r\n- [Timed Actions](./01-basics/timed-actions.lotnb)\r\n- [Topic Actions](./01-basics/topic-actions.lotnb)\r\n- [Conditional Logic](./02-logic/conditional-logic.lotnb)\r\n\r\n### Intermediate Level\r\n- [Basic Models](./03-models/basic-models.lotnb)\r\n- [Action Models](./03-models/action-models.lotnb)\r\n- [Model Inheritance](./03-models/model-inheritance.lotnb)\r\n- [MQTT Bridge](./04-routes/mqtt-bridge.lotnb)\r\n- [Database Routes](./04-routes/database-routes.lotnb)\r\n\r\n### Advanced Level\r\n- [Simple Python](./05-python/simple-python.lotnb)\r\n- [Advanced Python](./05-python/advanced-python.lotnb)\r\n\r\n</details>\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Welcome to LoT!\r\n\r\n**LoT (Language of Things)** is the SQL of real-time MQTT data. Just as SQL transforms and queries static database records, LoT transforms and processes live MQTT streams in real-time.\r\n\r\n### The LoT Revolution\r\n- **SQL**: `SELECT * FROM users WHERE age > 18` - Static data query\r\n- **LoT**: `ON TOPIC \"sensors/+\" IF PAYLOAD > 80 THEN...` - Real-time data processing\r\n\r\n**LoT eliminates the need for complex middleware** by embedding business logic directly into the MQTT broker. Your data flows, transforms, and reacts in real-time without external services, databases, or message queues.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n> **CAUTION - Free Tier Resource Limits**\r\n>\r\n> The free version of Coreflux has resource limits:\r\n> - **Routes**: 2 maximum\r\n> - **Actions**: 12 maximum\r\n> - **Models**: 40 maximum\r\n>\r\n> Delete unused resources before creating new ones during exercises.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Getting Started\r\n\r\n### One-Click Setup\r\n\r\nWe've made it easy! Just run the setup script and you're ready to go:\r\n\r\n**Windows (PowerShell):**\r\n```powershell\r\ncd 00-setup/setup\r\n.\\install-docker.ps1\r\n```\r\n\r\n**Linux/macOS (Terminal):**\r\n```bash\r\ncd 00-setup/setup\r\nchmod +x install-docker.sh\r\n./install-docker.sh\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe script will automatically:\r\n1. Check if Docker is installed (and guide you to install it if not)\r\n2. Start Docker if it's not running\r\n3. Pull and start the Coreflux MQTT Broker\r\n4. Display connection details when ready\r\n\r\n### [Environment Verification](./00-setup/verify-environment.lotnb)\r\n\r\nAfter running the setup script, open the [Environment Verification](./00-setup/verify-environment.lotnb) notebook to test your connection.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Learning Path\r\n\r\n### Beginner Level - Start Here!\r\n\r\n#### [1. Basic Concepts](./01-basics/)\r\n- **[Timed Actions](./01-basics/timed-actions.lotnb)** - Learn `ON EVERY` triggers\r\n- **[Topic Actions](./01-basics/topic-actions.lotnb)** - Master `ON TOPIC` events\r\n\r\n#### [2. Logic & Control](./02-logic/)\r\n- **[Conditional Logic](./02-logic/conditional-logic.lotnb)** - IF/ELSE statements and counters\r\n\r\n### Intermediate Level\r\n\r\n#### [3. Data Models](./03-models/)\r\n- **[Basic Models](./03-models/basic-models.lotnb)** - Model definitions and field types\r\n- **[Action Models](./03-models/action-models.lotnb)** - Publishing models from actions\r\n- **[Model Inheritance](./03-models/model-inheritance.lotnb)** - Extending models\r\n\r\n#### [4. System Integration](./04-routes/)\r\n- **[MQTT Bridge](./04-routes/mqtt-bridge.lotnb)** - Connect different brokers\r\n- **[Database Routes](./04-routes/database-routes.lotnb)** - Store data in PostgreSQL\r\n\r\n### Advanced Level\r\n\r\n#### [5. Python Integration](./05-python/)\r\n- **[Simple Python](./05-python/simple-python.lotnb)** - Basic CALL PYTHON usage\r\n- **[Advanced Python](./05-python/advanced-python.lotnb)** - Complex data processing\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Training Environment\r\n\r\nThis training includes a complete Docker-based simulation environment:\r\n\r\n| Service | Port | Purpose |\r\n|---------|------|--------|\r\n| Coreflux MQTT | 1883 | Primary LoT broker |\r\n| PostgreSQL | 5432 | Database exercises |\r\n| OPC UA Simulator | 4840 | Factory simulation |\r\n| Mosquitto | 1884 | Bridge exercises |\r\n| Adminer | 8080 | Database UI |\r\n\r\n**Public Cloud Services:**\r\n| Service | URL | Purpose |\r\n|---------|-----|--------|\r\n| Coreflux Cloud | iot.coreflux.cloud:1883 | Cloud bridge demos |\r\n| JSONPlaceholder | jsonplaceholder.typicode.com | REST API testing |\r\n| ReqRes | reqres.in/api | User management API |\r\n| Open-Meteo | api.open-meteo.com | Weather data |\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Learning Objectives\r\n\r\nBy the end of this training session, you will:\r\n\r\n- **Understand LoT fundamentals** - Actions, Models, Routes\r\n- **Build real-time data pipelines** - Process MQTT streams instantly\r\n- **Create industrial IoT solutions** - Connect databases, APIs, OPC UA\r\n- **Integrate Python processing** - Handle complex calculations\r\n- **Design scalable architectures** - Enterprise-ready patterns\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Prerequisites\r\n\r\n### Required\r\n- Docker Desktop installed and running\r\n- Basic understanding of MQTT concepts\r\n- Familiarity with JSON data structures\r\n\r\n### Recommended\r\n- Python programming experience\r\n- Database concepts (SQL)\r\n- REST API understanding\r\n\r\n### Setup\r\n\r\nJust run the setup script - it handles everything automatically!\r\n\r\n**Windows:** `cd 00-setup/setup && .\\install-docker.ps1`\r\n\r\n**Linux/macOS:** `cd 00-setup/setup && ./install-docker.sh`\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Quick Start Guide\r\n\r\n1. **Run Setup Script** - Execute the install script in `00-setup/setup/` (see above)\r\n2. **Verify Setup** - Complete [Environment Verification](./00-setup/verify-environment.lotnb)\r\n3. **Start Learning** - Begin with [Timed Actions](./01-basics/timed-actions.lotnb)\r\n4. **Practice** - Complete exercises in each tutorial\r\n5. **Experiment** - Modify examples and build your own solutions\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Tutorial Structure\r\n\r\nEach tutorial follows a consistent format:\r\n\r\n- **Introduction** - What you'll learn\r\n- **Concepts** - Core theory and syntax\r\n- **Hands-On Examples** - Working code with explanations\r\n- **Exercises** - Practice problems\r\n- **Summary** - Key takeaways\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Community & Support\r\n\r\n- **Documentation**: [docs.coreflux.org](https://docs.coreflux.org)\r\n- **Community**: [Discord Server](https://discord.com/invite/A3pPrptNMm)\r\n- **Examples**: [GitHub](https://github.com/CorefluxCommunity)\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Ready to Start?\r\n\r\n**Begin with [Environment Verification](./00-setup/verify-environment.lotnb) to ensure your setup is ready!**\r\n\r\nThen continue with [Timed Actions](./01-basics/timed-actions.lotnb) to start your LoT journey."
  }
